\chapter{Novostone and Firestone HIR integrations}
\label{ch:76}
\index{Novostone and Firestone HIR integrations}

The optional Novostone pass folds a bounded subset of closed checked expressions. The Firestone HIR pass supplies checked full-width integer folds and a divide-by-one rewrite within its documented subset. Each has an explicit CMake option and a named compiler optimization selector. These passes run before authored HIR rewrites. They work through checked adapters so the application needs no LibStone analysis runtime.

\section{Preserve traps and signed width}
Set up one build for each provider, record the selected option, and run equivalent source with the pass enabled and disabled. Use a successful full-width fold and an edge case that must trap or remain unoptimized. For division, check the boundary between a valid result and an invalid division before expecting constant replacement. Inspect generated artifacts and actual results. Firestone pattern compilation and the Novostone relational MIR analysis are separate capabilities, with distinct commands and phase boundaries in \cref{ch:20} and \cref{ch:86}.

